Store merged immediates to memory before moving registers.

A frame merge writes immediates to memory first, because the store needs a
spare register and getting one may spill a register mapped in the frame. Only
destinations held in memory alone were handled there. A destination cached in
a register as well got its memory store in the last loop, after other
locations had been moved into place. When no register was free, the spare
register could be one the target frame had just been given, such as the one
holding this, and the constant overwrote it.

Do the memory store of every immediate in the first loop; the register store
remains in the last loop.

--- a/cldc/src/vm/share/compiler/VirtualStackFrame.cpp
+++ b/cldc/src/vm/share/compiler/VirtualStackFrame.cpp
@@ -753,10 +753,12 @@
   FOR_EACH_LOCATION_DONE(src, dst, index);

   // Need to handle immediate->memory transfers in a separate loop,
-  // since this might allocate registers mapped in the frame.
+  // since this might allocate registers mapped in the frame. This
+  // includes the memory store for a destination that also keeps the value
+  // in a register: the register is written in the loop below.
   FOR_EACH_LOCATION_DO(src, dst, index)
-    if (dst->is_flushed() && src->is_immediate()) {
-      src->conform_to(index, dst, index);
+    if (src->is_immediate() && (dst->is_flushed() || !dst->is_immediate())) {
+      src->do_conform_to(index, dst, index, RawLocation::LOC_STORE);
     }
   FOR_EACH_LOCATION_DONE(src, dst, index);

